DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive session exploring how meaningful par
 tnerships between academic institutions and community organizations can st
 rengthen community health initiatives. Drawing on lessons from Project GRA
 CE\, a community-academic partnership with more than 20 years of experienc
 e in eastern North Carolina\, presenters will share practical strategies f
 or community engagement\, relationship building\, shared decision-making\,
  and sustainable collaboration. Participants will gain a better understand
 ing of community-engaged and participatory research approaches and leave w
 ith actionable ideas for applying these principles in their own work.\n\n 
 \n\nRegister for Building Partnerships! \n\n \n\nPresenters are Mysha Wynn
 \, Erika Redding and Mary McKinley. \n\n \n\nThis session is part of the C
 onnections that Count: Abacus Evaluation Community Engagement Webinar Seri
 es.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Building Effective Community-Academic Partnerships: Lessons from Pr
 oject GRACE
