DESCRIPTION:At this meeting\, we will highlight recent policy and procedure
  changes and demonstrate enhancements to systems that support sponsored pr
 ogram administration\, including ALICE\, RAM Tracker\, and RAMSeS. Using p
 roposal and agreement submission examples\, we will walk through the full 
 request lifecycle\, illustrating how requests are initiated\, routed\, rev
 iewed\, and tracked in RAMSeS and RAM Tracker\, including the visibility a
 vailable to departments throughout the process.\n\n \n\nThis meeting requi
 res UNC-CH email authentication. If you have difficulty registering\, log 
 into Zoom with Single Sign-On at https://unc.zoom.us/profile and click on 
 the profile icon in the top right-hand corner to find which email address 
 to use to register.\n\n \n\nThe Research Administrators Peer-to-Peer (RAPP
 ) group seeks to create a community of practice for research administrator
 s and other professionals involved in research administration across the U
 niversity of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. The group will participate in 
 meetings and other activities to inform\, educate\, and support individual
 s by providing a forum for discussion and an open exchange of ideas\; an i
 nformation network for policies\, procedures\, and sponsor guidelines\; an
 d networking opportunities for research administration professionals acros
 s campus.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:RAPP Session: RAMSeS Enhancements
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/rapp-session-ramses-enhancemen
 ts
END:VEVENT
