DESCRIPTION:From the mountains to the coast – North Carolina’s climate 
 is changing. One aspect of the climate system that is of concern is the fr
 equency\, intensity\, and duration of extreme heat and rainfall events.\n\
 n \n\nIn September's Carolina Science Cafe\, State Climatologist & Directo
 r of the State Climate Office of NC Jared H. Bowden\, PhD\, will discuss o
 bserved changes in extreme heat and rainfall\, the climate science that su
 pports these changes\, and provide insight into the future using climate m
 odels.\n\n \n\n🎟️ Free and open to adults\n\n🍴 Light appetizers av
 ailable for attendees\n\n🍻 Drinks available for purchase\n\n \n\n📍Ho
 sted by Morehead Planetarium at Haw River Tap & Table in Carrboro.
GEO:35.910154;-79.068833
LOCATION:Haw River Tap & Table
SUMMARY:Carolina Science Cafe: NC’s Changing Climate
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/carolina-science-cafe-ncs-chan
 ging-climate
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
