DESCRIPTION:Campus labs and research are incredibly important to the Univer
 sity\, but they're also very water and energy intensive. In fact\, campus 
 labs are the largest consumers of water and energy on campus. Started in 2
 009 as the Green Labs program\, Sustainable Carolina has revamped the prog
 ram and given it a new name: Sustainable Labs.\n\n \n\nThe program focuses
  on key areas (waste\, energy and water\, freezers\, chemicals)\, and is d
 esigned not to shame labs or lab personnel for waste or energy intensive e
 quipment\, but rather to identify small steps labs can take to be more sus
 tainable and to recognize all the steps that labs have already taken.\n\n 
 \n\nThis interest session for Sustainable Labs will be led by Langley Smit
 h\, Sustainable Carolina’s program specialist. We invite lab managers\, 
 students who work in labs\, and faculty to join us and learn how their lab
 s can participate in the program.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Sustainable Labs Interest Session
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/sustainable-labs-interest-sess
 ion
