DESCRIPTION:This interactive online workshop will focus on semi-structured 
 interviewing\, a data collection method used in qualitative research. Topi
 cs covered will include basics of semi-structured interviews\, development
  of interview questions and probes\, interviewing skills\, and considerati
 ons for conducting virtual interviews. Participants will have the opportun
 ity to practice developing interview questions and using interviewing skil
 ls.\n\n \n\nThis event is part of the NC TraCS Qualitative Research Traini
 ng Series and may be recorded. Materials such as slides or handouts will b
 e shared with documented attendees only.\n\n \n\nPresenters:\nMaryBeth Gre
 we\, MPH\nProgram Manager\, Qualitative Research Service\nResearch Special
 ist\, Patient and Community Engagement in Research (PaCER) Program\n\n \n\
 nSimone Frank\, MPH\nSenior Project Manager\, Patient and Community Engage
 ment in Research (PaCER) Program\nResearch Specialist\, Qualitative Resear
 ch Service\n\n \n\nRegister\n\n \n\nPlease contact MaryBeth Grewe at maryb
 eth_grewe@med.unc.edu if you have questions about this training.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Semi-Structured Interviewing
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/semi-structured-interviewing-3
 284
