DESCRIPTION:Curious about how to use generative AI (genAI) to inform your c
 linical research and practice? This session will cover the basics of using
  genAI chatbots and AI-assisted tools for clinical information retrieval a
 nd literature reviews. We’ll discuss the pros and cons of using AI tools
  for different steps of the research process\, prompting strategies\, and 
 using GenAI for evidence reviews. A review of clinical genAI tools will be
  included.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the UNC Health Sciences Lib
 rary and is led by Luke Barron\, Joel Collier\, and Beth Moreton. It is pa
 rt of the For Clinicians: Enhancing Practice Through Knowledge and Advanci
 ng Clinical Research Skills workshop tracks.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:GenAI Tools and Resources in the Clinical Setting
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/genai-tools-and-resources-in-t
 he-clinical-setting
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041912Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52682468786866
DTSTART:20260916T190000Z
DTEND:20260916T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:In this course\, we will cover basic Qualtrics functions beginn
 ing with an overview of survey options and settings\, followed by hands-on
  practice programming and distributing a survey and downloading results. W
 e will program some of the most common question and response types\, custo
 mize requirements and validation\, and add display logic\, skip logic\, an
 d basic branch logic in the “survey flow”. We will then create and upl
 oad a contact list and discuss advantages and disadvantages of distributin
 g the survey with a single reusable link vs. the survey mailer.  Finally\,
  we will cover a basic overview of the Data & Analysis tab for viewing\, e
 diting\, and exporting raw data into various formats including .csv\, .tsv
 \, .excel\, and .spss. Other topics include project sharing/ collaboration
 \, Groups and Libraries\, and preventing fraudulent responses and bot acti
 vity.\n\nRegistration and fee are required for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Qualtrics
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-qualtrics-9208
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
