DESCRIPTION:Learn more about the history of the nation’s first public uni
 versity by attending a Carolina History Tour. The Carolina History Tours c
 over more than 200 years of the history of UNC-Chapel Hill\, including the
  establishment of the university in the 18th century\, the history of camp
 us landmarks including the Old Well\, Davie Poplar\, and Unsung Founders M
 emorial\, the push to open enrollment to all North Carolinians\, and the g
 rowth of the school in the 20th and 21st centuries. Tours will begin at th
 e Old Well and finish at Wilson Library. Most tours last a little over an 
 hour. \n\nLed by staff from the Wilson Special Collections Library\, these
  tours are part of the University Library’s commitment to collecting\, p
 reserving\, and sharing the history of the University of North Carolina at
  Chapel Hill. \n\nRegistration is required. You can register for your spot
  here.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Carolina History Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/carolina-history-tour-7788
CATEGORIES:Tours
END:VEVENT
