DTSTART:20260922T180000Z
DTEND:20260922T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:QGIS is one of the most widely used open source GIS software pl
 atforms\, with a range of applications that include business analytics\, n
 atural and health sciences\, transportation\, and more. Its suite of tools
  offers capabilities for data visualization\, data management\, spatial an
 alysis\, map creation\, and more. This hands-on course for beginners will 
 provide an overview of QGIS\, including its layout and capabilities. Topic
 s covered will include importing geographic data\, styling and symbolizing
  data\, querying and selecting data\, making basic maps\, and more!\n\n \n
 \nThis workshop is offered by the University Library and will be led by Ph
 ilip McDaniel and Gracie Riehm. \n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered re
 motely via Zoom. Register here: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/event/1722917
 0
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to QGIS
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-qgis
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53798217063455
DTSTART:20260922T210000Z
DTEND:20260922T223000Z
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of National Forensic Science Week 2026\, what ex
 actly is forensic science\, and how is it used in the real world? Join us 
 for an introduction to the science behind forensic investigations and expl
 ore the many ways forensic science is applied to analyze evidence and supp
 ort investigations and put your forensic science skills to the test in thi
 s interactive case investigation! During this event\, you’ll be presente
 d with the details of a fictional case and challenged to work alongside th
 e people around you to evaluate key aspects of the investigation and piece
  together what happened. As the case unfolds\, you’ll tackle different f
 orensic science questions\, discuss your findings with your team\, and use
  critical thinking and collaboration to work toward a final conclusion. Ca
 n you work the case and figure out what happened? Join us for Let’s Work
  a Case and find out!
GEO:35.908258;-79.050937
LOCATION:Coker Hall\, 215
SUMMARY:Let's Work a Case
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/lets-work-a-case
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
