DESCRIPTION:Collecting data is now easier than it has ever been. But\, as d
 ata becomes more prolific\, datasets become larger and more complex. How d
 o we find meaningful patterns in our data? How can we communicate those pa
 tterns to others? Data visualization allows us to make sense of today’s 
 ever evolving information landscape.\n\n \n\nThis workshop will introduce 
 the history and basic principles of data visualization. Learn about best p
 ractices and resources for making an impact with your data through compell
 ing charts\, graphs\, and maps. At the end of the short course\, participa
 nts will be able to:\n\nUnderstand the preattentive process and how it aff
 ects visual perceptionCritically evaluate the accuracy and quality of visu
 alizations they encounter in their daily livesImplement best practices whe
 n creating their own visualizations \n\nThis workshop is offered by the Un
 iversity Library and will be led by librarian Lorin Bruckner. \n\n \n\nThi
 s workshop is being offered remotely via Zoom. Register here: https://cale
 ndar.lib.unc.edu/event/17236339
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Making an Impact with Data Viz
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/making-an-impact-with-data-viz
 -160
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
