UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53701638569831
DTSTART:20260924T161000Z
DTEND:20260924T171000Z
DESCRIPTION:On Sept. 24\, English and comparative literature professor Step
 hanie Elizondo Griest (FFP ’15\, ’23) will give a Fellows Forum presen
 tation titled\, “Art is Everything.”\n\nIs art enough?\n\n\nAll artist
 s struggle. But women are especially pushed to give up their creative ambi
 tions\, from societal disapproval against “selfishness” to the pressur
 e (or desire) for children and economic stability. After spending much of 
 her twenties and thirties wondering if prioritizing her writing over every
 thing else was leading her to fulfillment or regret\, Stephanie Elizondo G
 riest turned to other women for their perspectives on that haunting questi
 on: is art enough? Her 2025 book Art Above Everything documents her travel
 s to 10 nations—from Cuba to Iceland\; Rwanda to Qatar—where she inter
 views legendary painters\, poets\, actors\, dancers\, and musicians who ta
 lk intimately about their art\, both what it gifts them and what it costs 
 them. Join us for a multi-media presentation and discussion about the real
 ities of placing art at the core of your existence.\n\nIntroductions will 
 begin at 12:10. The presentation will be from 12:15 – 12:45 p.m.\, with 
 a Q&A session to follow. Refreshments will be served.\n\nRSVP for the Fell
 ows Forum on Jotform.\n\n \n\nSee all events in the IAH Fellows Forum seri
 es.
GEO:35.913407;-79.052875
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, University Room
SUMMARY:IAH Fellows Forum: Art is Everything
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/iah-fellows-forum-art-is-every
 thing
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
