UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53576663164391
DTSTART:20260924T223000Z
DTEND:20260924T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Jamaica Gilmer is a relentless hope-architect\, multifaceted ar
 tist\, and curator working\nacross photography\, ceramics\, and film. Her 
 most recent series\, We are the Sun: A\nPhotographic Tribute to Black Comm
 unity\, celebrates the intergenerational wisdom of\nThirdSpace Action Lab 
 in Cleveland\, Ohio. She is the founder of The Beautiful Project\n(TBP) an
 d the lead curator of TBP’s past exhibition at the Metropolitan Museum o
 f Art’s\nUris Center for Education\, Pen\, Lens\, and Soul: The Story of
  The Beautiful Project. Her\nwork is featured in Kleaver Cruz’s recent b
 ook\, The Black Joy Project: A Literary and\nVisual Love Letter to How We 
 Thrive. At the core of her organizing practice\, Jamaica is\ncommitted to 
 telling sacred stories of possibility through interdisciplinary making.\n\
 n\nRead more about the artist: www.jamaicagilmer.com\n\n \n\nReverence: Ha
 ir Memory Through Images by Jamaica Gilmer is a photographic\ntestament to
  Black hair. Here\, stylists and barbers become the hair artists\, and the
 \nBlack people who sit in their chairs become the muse. This exhibition ce
 lebrates the\nlong-held tradition of being immersed in images while you wa
 it for your turn in the chair.\nLook-books filled with style options\, wal
 ls adorned with even more—our global histories\npresented as sacred exhi
 bitions in everyday spaces.\n\n \n\nCheck out this exclusive Exhibition Op
 ening and Artist Talk on September 24th\, 2026 at the Robert and Sallie Br
 own Gallery at the Sonja Haynes Stone Center!
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, The Robert and Sallie Brown Gallery and Museum 
SUMMARY:Exhibition – Reverence: Hair Memory Through Images
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/exhibition-reverence-hair-memo
 ry-through-images
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
