DESCRIPTION:R is a free and open-source way to explore and analyze data\, i
 ncluding spatial data. In this workshop\, we will introduce you to spatial
  analysis and visualization techniques in RStudio. We will use packages li
 ke sf\, tidycensus\, tigris\, terra\, and more to demonstrate typical GIS 
 workflows and produce basic maps.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is designed for pa
 rticipants with some familiarity with R/RStudio and/or GIS. If you need so
 me additional background\, feel free to join our beginR series or our ArcG
 IS Pro for Beginners workshop earlier in the semester\n\n \n\nThis worksho
 p is offered by the University Libraries and will be led by librarians Phi
 lip McDaniel and Matthew Jansen. \n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered r
 emotely via Zoom only. Register here: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/event/1
 7229736
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Working with Spatial Data in R
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/working-with-spatial-data-in-r
 -2598
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
