DTEND:20260929T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:During this workshop\, participants will be provided useful tip
 s and tools for optimizing the reach of their work. Attendees will gain a 
 series of strategic skills to help ensure their published research reaches
  a wide audience and its research impact can be tracked.\n\nTopics covered
  will include:\n\nResearch impact measurement optionsOptimizing abstract w
 riting for database discoverabilityWriting a plain language summary of a s
 tudyBenefits of ORCID and how to set up an ORCIDUnderstanding open access 
 publishing and author rights \n\nGraduate students and post-docs from all 
 disciplines are welcome.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the UNC Healt
 h Sciences Library through the Graduate School and led by Emma Barrett-Cat
 ton. It is part of the For Researchers and Advancing Clinical Research Ski
 lls workshop tracks.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Maximizing Your Research Impact (Graduate School Event)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/maximizing-your-research-impac
 t-graduate-school-event
