UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53107832352974
DTSTART:20260930T160000Z
DTEND:20260930T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Managing individuals who may be struggling with stress\, anxiet
 y\, depression and other mental health concerns can be a difficult balanci
 ng act. Your role is to manage performance and to bring out the best in yo
 ur workforce\, but accomplishing this often requires you to express concer
 n and support when employees struggle emotionally. Managers often feel unc
 omfortable in this aspect of their role and may lack the important skills 
 of “emotional management.” This course covers ways employees may prese
 nt their distress and offers insights and strategies on forging supportive
  empathic alliances within the role of manager. The session also identifie
 s common mistakes managers make in responding to employees in distress and
  explains communication skills that express support and convey positive ex
 pectancy. Participants are also given information on how to refer employee
 s to the Employee Assistance Program.\n\n \n\nClick on Carolina Talent reg
 istration link and select the “Request” button to automatically enroll
 .
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Mental Health Awareness for Leaders
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/mental-health-awareness-for-le
 aders-4528
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
