DESCRIPTION:Tableau is a user-friendly software application used to create 
 static or interactive visualizations and dashboards. Examples can be found
  here.\n\n \n\nTableau’s drag-and-drop interface provides tools to build
  a variety of visualizations with no coding required\, and visualizations 
 can be embedded in websites by copying and pasting embed code. Attendees w
 ill get started with Tableau in this hands on workshop by learning how to 
 import data\, create basic charts and maps\, make and publish dashboards\,
  and more!\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University Library and 
 will be led by librarian Lorin Bruckner. \n\n \n\nThis workshop is being o
 ffered remotely via Zoom. Register here: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/even
 t/17236362
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Tableau I
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/tableau-i-1771
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
