DESCRIPTION:Learning R on your own? Want some help along the way? beginR is
  a series of virtual meetings organized by the University Libraries and th
 e Odum Institute that provides support to students\, faculty and staff who
  are learning the R programming language. The first week\, the instructors
  will introduce attendees to R\, help them install the software\, and shar
 e the materials that will be covered in subsequent meetings. In the follow
 ing weeks\, beginR attendees will learn R by following the lessons on the 
 R Open Labs website at their own pace. Each week\, staff will be available
  via Zoom to answer questions\, solve problems and provide the solutions t
 o exercises.\n\n \n\nbeginR is a collaboration between the University Libr
 ary and the Odum Institute. The workshops will be led by librarians Lorin 
 Bruckner and Matt Jansen\, and Nuvan Rathnayaka from the Odum Institute. \
 n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered remotely via Zoom only. Register he
 re: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/event/17229647
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:beginR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/beginr-3408
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52259576347604
DTSTART:20261001T170000Z
DTEND:20261001T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:AI in Research: Driving Innovation Forward\n\nDiscover how arti
 ficial intelligence can streamline workflows\, uncover hidden patterns\, a
 nd empower breakthroughs in your field. Learn practical applications of AI
  through Odum Institute AIR series that can revolutionize your research pr
 ocess.\n\nAI\, for example ChatGPT\, may be used to carry out some tasks c
 ommonly used by social scientists. Examples include Pearson’s chi-square
  test\, Fisher’s exact test\, Student’s t-test\, power calculations an
 d non-centrality parameters. The quality of responses has varied to this p
 oint and may continue to at the time of the class. Examples will be given.
 \n\nYou must have a UNC Chapel Hill Onyen to register and attend this cour
 se. No registration fees required but you must register to secure your spo
 t and receive the Zoom link.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI in Research Series – AI and Simple Statistics
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-research-series-ai-and-s
 imple-statistics-2484
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53797518116711
DTSTART:20261001T180000Z
DTEND:20261001T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Generative AI can reflect human bias through the data it is tra
 ined on\, the choices made by its developers\, and the ways we use it. The
  good news is that we can take steps to reduce that bias. In this workshop
 \, you’ll learn how to write thoughtful prompts\, question AI-generated 
 responses\, and guide GenAI tools toward more balanced and reliable result
 s.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University Libraries and will b
 e led by librarian Michele Hayslett.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offere
 d remotely via Zoom only. You can register through the library calendar. R
 egistrants will receive a Zoom link\; those on the waitlist will not recei
 ve a Zoom link unless they are bumped up to a registered spot.\n\n\nAll re
 gistrants however\, will receive access to the meeting recording and resou
 rces.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Mitigating Bias in AI
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/mitigating-bias-in-ai-1299
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
