DESCRIPTION:This course is only open to the UNC Chapel Hill Community. You 
 must have an active ONYEN to register. \n\nPlease note: Registration is fo
 r INDIVIDUAL Attendee only so we can track capacity. Attendance is require
 d as it will not be recorded.\n\nAI for Research (AIR)\, a collaboration b
 etween the Odum Institute and the University Library: Driving Innovation F
 orward\n\nDiscover how artificial intelligence can streamline workflows\, 
 uncover hidden patterns\, and empower breakthroughs in your field. Learn p
 ractical applications of AI through Odum Institute AIR series that can rev
 olutionize your research process.\n\nThis course will introduce participan
 ts to generative AI tools in qualitative software—ATLAS.ti\, MAXQDA\, an
 d NVivo. These tools can be used to summarize textual documents through AI
 -assisted memo writing and to support coding\, with each program taking a 
 different approach to integrating human judgment and AI features.\n\nThe c
 ourse will also demonstrate how ChatGPT can be used to code textual data\,
  how to create effective prompts\, and how to import results from ChatGPT 
 into qualitative software for further analysis. The course will be based o
 n presentation and lecture but will provide brief exercises for hands-on e
 xercises to be completed outside of the course.\n\nThis course is eligible
  for CLE credit and CEU credit.\n\nYou must have a UNC Chapel Hill Onyen t
 o register and attend this course. No registration fees required but you m
 ust register to secure your spot and receive the Zoom link.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI for Research – Introduction to AI Tools in Qualitative Softwar
 e
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-for-research-introduction-t
 o-ai-tools-in-qualitative-software
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
