DESCRIPTION:The AI for Research (AIR) workshop series is a collaboration be
 tween the Odum Institute and the University Library. \n\n \n\nWant to know
  how generative AI (GenAI) can be used to support your research? This work
 shop covers various GenAI tools that have applications for research tasks 
 including tools that support writing manuscripts\, exploring and summarizi
 ng literature (e.g.\, Research Rabbit\, Consensus\, and Undermind)\, perfo
 rming data analysis (e.g.\, Julius and ProQuest TDM Studio)\, and conducti
 ng evidence syntheses (including systematic and scoping reviews). An overv
 iew of library resources that support GenAI including PromptLab and the Li
 brary AI Studio is also provided.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is intended for th
 ose with some existing knowledge of genAI. If you need more of an introduc
 tion to AI\, please check out the Library's other AI-related workshops.\n\
 n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the Odum Institute and the University Li
 brary and will be led by Luke Barron and Katherine Howell.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI for Research: Leveraging Generative AI for Research Tasks
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-for-research-leveraging-gen
 erative-ai-for-research-tasks
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
