DTSTART:20261013T230000Z
DTEND:20261014T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:When was the last time a performance changed the way you looked
  at the world around you? \n\nVoice of Nature: the Anthropocene is an expl
 oration of one of the defining issues of our time—environmental change
 —through music and imagery. It invites us to consider the beauty and fra
 gility of the natural world and our relationship to it.\n\nPerformed by ac
 claimed soprano Renée Fleming\, the program pairs classical songs and con
 temporary works with an original film created in partnership with the Nati
 onal Geographic Society. The experience is both intimate and expansive\, s
 haring landscapes of breathtaking beauty alongside acute reminders of thei
 r vulnerability.\n\n \n\nAt a moment when environmental change increasingl
 y shapes everyday life\, Voice of Nature reminds us that these challenges 
 are not just scientific or political\; they are deeply personal. It is an 
 invitation to consider how rapidly the natural world is changing while ref
 lecting on how much we rely on its constancy for solace\, inspiration\, an
 d a sense of connection to something larger than ourselves.\n\n \n\nStuden
 t tickets always $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets  at:
  https://carolinaperformingarts.org/events/voice-of-nature/
LOCATION:Memorial Hal
SUMMARY:Renée Fleming in Recital Voice of Nature: the Anthropocene
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/renee-fleming-in-recital-voice
 -of-nature-the-anthropocene
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
