DESCRIPTION:Join the UNC Hussman Political Communication Focus Program for 
 a fireside chat featuring former White House press secretary Jen Psaki\, m
 oderated by Jennifer Davis\, Knott Distinguished Professor of the Practice
  in the UNC Curriculum in Peace\, War and Defense.\n\n \n\nAbout Jen Psaki
 \n\nPsaki is the anchor of MS NOW’s “The Briefing with Jen Psaki” an
 d host of the MS NOW original podcast “The Blueprint with Jen Psaki.”\
 n\n \n\nThe former White House press secretary for President Joe Biden was
  lauded by the Associated Press as a communicator who “dug deep into pol
 icy\, seeking an understanding that goes far beyond talking points\,” an
 d was celebrated for bringing “a mixture of warmth\, humor\, intelligenc
 e and edge” to her role by Vogue.\n\n \n\nPrior to her time in the Biden
  White House\, Psaki was a longtime adviser to President Barack Obama and 
 served as a traveling press secretary on his first long-shot campaign\, an
 d later served as the White House communications director.\n\n \n\nAdditio
 nally\, Psaki also served as the administration’s public face on the glo
 bal stage during her tenure as the State Department spokesperson\, traveli
 ng the world with Secretary of State John Kerry. Psaki is also the author 
 of “Say More: Lessons from Work\, the White House\, and the World” (Sc
 ribner\, 2024).\n\n \n\nPsaki graduated from the College of William & Mary
  with a double major in English and sociology. While at William & Mary\, s
 he was a member of the swim team\, Chi Omega sorority and was involved in 
 several other campus programs and activities. \n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\nThis ev
 ent is hosted by the UNC Hussman School of Journalism and Media and is ope
 n to all. UNC students can register for CLE credit on Heel Life.
GEO:35.907828;-79.054177
LOCATION:FedEx Global Education Center\, Nelson Mandela Auditorium
SUMMARY:Fireside Chat with Jen Psaki
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/fireside-chat-with-jen-psaki
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
