DTSTART:20261021T170000Z
DTEND:20261021T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Brain Chemistry and ADHD: What We Know and Where We Are Headed\
 n\nBrain structure and brain chemistry are crucial components to understan
 ding ADHD and its treatment.  Greg Mattingly\, M.D.\, is the President of 
 the American Professional Society of ADHD and Related Disorders (APSARD)\,
  has served as consultant to both the NFL and MLB\, and is Co-Chair of the
  U.S. Psych Congress. He has extensively researched ADHD and taught psycho
 pharmacology for more than 20 years. In this seminar he will bring his wea
 lth of knowledge and expertise to present what is known about brain functi
 on and ADHD\, including how various brain chemicals such as dopamine\, nor
 epinephrine\, and serotonin are involved. He will offer current research f
 indings\, will address how medications to treat ADHD are related to brain 
 neuroanatomy and neurotransmitters\, and will discuss new and upcoming med
 ication options. The presentation will also include information on brain n
 europlasticity\, environmental influences\, accompanying diagnoses\, and t
 he new adult guidelines for diagnosing ADHD.
GEO:35.912385;-79.004586
LOCATION:Rizzo Center\, Magnolia
