DESCRIPTION:Join the University Library and the Department of History for a
  special exhibition viewing and public talk commemorating America's 250th 
 anniversary. Katheen DuVal\, Carl W. Ernst Distinguished Professor of Hist
 ory at UNC-Chapel Hill and recipient of a 2025 Pulitzer Prize for Native N
 ations: A Millennium in North America\, will share insights into American 
 history. The evening will include viewing of the Wilson Library exhibition
  "Witnesses to the Revolution: North Carolina and the War for Independence
 \,” produced in partnership with the North Carolina Museum of History.
LOCATION:Wilson Library\, Fearrington Reading Room
SUMMARY:An evening with historian Kathleen DuVal 
