DESCRIPTION:This session provides an overview of searching methodology and 
 best practices for systematic and other comprehensive reviews. Topics incl
 ude translating research questions into searchable concepts\, choosing dat
 abases and information sources\, developing search strategies\, and docume
 nting searches for reproducibility and transparency.\n\n \n\nThis workshop
  is offered by the UNC Health Sciences Library and led by Joel Collier. It
  is part of the Systematic Review Methods\, For Researchers\, For Clinicia
 ns: Enhancing Practice Through Knowledge\, and Advancing Clinical Research
  Skills workshop tracks.
