DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the UNC Hussman School of Journalism and Media\, the 
 fall 2026 Price Cone Liptzin Lecture will feature alumnus Guy Mossman ’0
 4 (M.A.)\, an American cinematographer whose work bridges intimate charact
 er study with bold\, cinematic visuals.\n\n \n\nMossman made his first sho
 rt film while serving in the Peace Corps in Paraguay in 2000 and went on t
 o earn a Park Fellowship at UNC-Chapel Hill\, completing a master’s degr
 ee focused on journalism and documentary filmmaking. \n\n \n\nHe is known 
 for his dramatic\, natural-light photography on award-winning documentarie
 s including the Oscar-shortlisted Sundance Audience Award winner “Buck\,
 ” the Sundance Special Jury Prize-winning “Feels Good Man” and “Be
 nding the Arc.”\n\n \n\nIn 2022\, he made his directorial debut co-direc
 ting and lensing “The Human Trial\,” an ambitious\, years-long chronic
 le of a radical Type 1 diabetes clinical trial. Most recently\, he co-dire
 cted\, produced and photographed SPEAK.\, a feature documentary that premi
 ered at the 2025 Sundance Film Festival\, following teenage competitive or
 ators at the National Speech & Debate Association’s championship as they
  discover the power of their voices through oratory and storytelling.\n\n 
 \n\nRegistration\n\nRSVP on Eventbrite\n\nUNC students can register for CL
 E credit on Heel Life\n\n \n\nAbout Mary Jane Price and Annie Cone Liptzin
 \n\nThe visual communication alumni-in-residence series was created in hon
 or of Mary Jane Price and Annie Cone Liptzin\, alumnae who volunteered for
  nearly a decade to assist with the darkroom\, equipment checkout and othe
 r needs of the UNC Hussman visual journalism program beginning in the 1980
 s.
GEO:35.909113;-79.052767
LOCATION:Carroll Hall\, Knight Learning Lab (Carroll Hall 111)
SUMMARY:Price Cone Liptzin Lecture with Guy Mossman
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/price-cone-liptzin-lecture-wit
 h-guy-mossman
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
