DTSTAMP:20260905T041914Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52242577665852
DTSTART:20261028T130000Z
DTEND:20261028T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course features Dynamic Narrative Inquiry – theory and p
 rinciples for narrative research design and analysis drawing on the richne
 ss of expressive language. With this approach to qualitative inquiry\, res
 earchers can build on communication in daily life where diverse practices 
 for sharing experience\, making sense of experience\, and imagining social
  change occur in personal narratives\, sociocultural communications\, and 
 institutional policies.\n\nThis course involves a sequence of presentation
 s and practical workshops with narrative analysis strategies applicable to
  small or large studies that sample verbal and/or visual discourse. We beg
 in with an introduction to dynamic narrative inquiry\, followed by modules
  with three analysis strategies that yield findings to a wide range of rel
 evant social science research questions. With examples from prior publishe
 d studies\, I present rationales and methodology\, including character map
 ping (to identify meaning in narrative actors\, actions\, and relationship
 s)\; plot analysis (to identify how narrative structures express logics an
 d intentions)\; and values analysis (to identify speaker/author/ purposes)
 . The final hour of the day is devoted to discussing course participants
 ’ insights from the workshops and implications for future research\, pra
 ctice\, and policy.\n\nRegistration and fee (refundable for students) are 
 required for Zoom link.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Narrative Analysis for the Qualitative Researcher (online)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/narrative-analysis-for-the-qua
 litative-researcher-online
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041914Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53693442664355
DTSTART:20261028T140000Z
DTEND:20261028T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Strengthening Engagement in Research: Building and Maintaining 
 Relationships with Patient & Community Partners\n\n \n\nMeaningful partner
 ships with patients\, community members\, or other collaborators involved 
 in your research are invaluable. Projects are set up for success when care
  is intentionally given to developing and strengthening partnerships over 
 time.\n\n \n\nThis online training will describe best practices for buildi
 ng mutually beneficial partnerships. The session will also cover common ch
 allenges that researchers and patient\, community\, and other partners exp
 erience when working together\, along with suggested solutions.\n\n \n\nPa
 rticipation in our Engagement in Research 101 or Engagement in Research Nu
 ts and Bolts trainings are not required to attend this session\; however\,
  some knowledge of engagement\, whether from prior training(s) or personal
  experience\, may foster deeper understanding of the material in this sess
 ion.\n\n \n\nRegister\n\n \n\nPresenters:\nAlicia Bilheimer\, MPH - Direct
 or of Engaged Science\, NC TraCS\nVeronica Carlisle\, MPH\, CHES - Senior 
 Community Health Educator\, UNC Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Center (LC
 CC)\nNisha Datta\, MS - Senior Project Manager\, NC TraCS\nSimone Frank\, 
 MPH - Senior Project Manager\, NC TraCS\nJennifer Potter\, MPH\, CHES - Se
 nior Program Coordinator for Clinical Outreach\, LCCC\nMembers of the NC T
 raCS Community and Patient Advisory Board and the UNC Lineberger Community
  Advisory Board\n\n \n\nEngaging Patient\, Community\, and Other Partners 
 in Your Research is a multi-part online training series. You may register 
 for the entire series OR any single training session. This training series
  was developed collaboratively with patient\, community\, and researcher p
 artners and is co-sponsored by the UNC Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Cen
 ter and NC TraCS Institute.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Strengthening Engagement in Research
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/strengthening-engagement-in-re
 search
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
