DESCRIPTION:On Oct. 30\, American studies assistant professor Antonia Rando
 lph (FFP ’22) will give a Fellows Forum presentation titled\, “It’s 
 all love? Beyoncé and Jay-Z and the Re-enchantment of Black Romance in th
 e Age of the Manosphere.”\n\n \n\nAntonia Randolph is the Jonathan M. He
 ss Career Development Term Assistant Professor at the University of North 
 Carolina-Chapel Hill. Her interests include diversity discourse in educati
 on\, Black feminist thought\, non-normative Black masculinity and sexualit
 y\, and hip-hop culture. Her book The Wrong Kind of Different: Challenging
  the Meaning of Diversity in American Classrooms (Teachers College 2012) e
 xamined the hierarchies elementary school teachers constructed among stude
 nts of color. Her current book project\, That’s My Heart: Queering Intim
 acy in Hip-Hop Culture\, forthcoming from University of California Press\,
  examines portrayals of Black men’s intimate relationships in hip-hop cu
 lture.\n\nRSVP for the Fellows Forum on Jotform.\n\nSee all events in the 
 IAH Fellows Forum series.
GEO:35.913374;-79.052866
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, University Room
SUMMARY:IAH Fellows Forum: Antonia Randolph
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/iah-fellows-forum-its-all-love
 -beyonce-and-jay-z-and-the-re-enchantment-of-black-romance-in-the-age-of-t
 he-manosphere
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
