DTSTART:20261030T230000Z
DTEND:20261031T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:The night before Halloween\, Memorial Hall transforms into some
 thing unsettling and mysterious. \n\n \n\nBefore the performance even begi
 ns\, audiences are invited to enter BARDO\, a haunting\, liminal place bet
 ween death and rebirth. Come dressed in your Halloween finest and venture 
 through spaces rarely open to audiences. Eerie installations. Strange enco
 unters. Unsettling imagery. Around every corner\, the sense that something
  is waiting—and watching—just out of sight. North Carolina performers 
 bring this dreamscape to life to create an experience that haunts long aft
 er the night is over. \n\n \n\nThe journey culminates with BLACK LODGE\, a
  dark Lynchian goth-rock opera about a tormented writer trapped in the nig
 htmarish Bardo\, where he is forced to confront the darkest moment of his 
 life again and again. Through the blending of music\, theater\, and film\,
  the performance explores what it means to reckon with the worst thing you
  have ever done. Together\, the two experiences create an evening that fee
 ls less like attending a traditional performance and more like stepping in
 to a collective late-night fever dream. Enter if you dare. \n\n \n\n*This 
 two-part event begins with BARDO at 7 p.m.\, followed by BLACK LODGE at 9 
 p.m. A single ticket includes both experiences.\n\n \n\n*Get in on the spi
 rit of horror movies and Halloween – audience members are encouraged to 
 arrive in costume!\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. Eligible for CLE. F
 ind out more and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperformingarts.org/events
 /blacklodgeandbardo/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:BLACK LODGE and BARDO
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/black-lodge-and-bardo
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
