DTEND:20261113T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Sankai Juku creates work that unfolds slowly and deliberately\,
  into what can feel like a new world\, where forces like time and gravity 
 seem to act on us in radically new ways.\n\n \n\nIn TOTEM: Void and Height
 \, dancers move with extraordinary presence and precision. Practicing the 
 Japanese dance tradition of Butoh\, the company’s performances exist som
 ehow between stillness and action\, between gravity and transcendence—an
 d sometimes feel less like watching dance and more like stepping inside a 
 waking dream. \n\n \n\nThe final work choreographed by their founder Ushio
  Amagatsu before his death in 2024\, TOTEM: Void and Height reflects a lif
 elong exploration of the relationship between the human body\, the natural
  world\, and the forces that shape them both. Through striking imagery and
  breathtaking physical control\, the performance invites audiences to slow
  down\, pay attention\, and experience time differently.\n\n \n\nThis is a
  rare opportunity to encounter one of the world’s most influential conte
 mporary dance companies and the final artistic vision of the artist who sh
 aped it for more than five decades.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. El
 igible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperformi
 ngarts.org/events/totem/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:Sankai Juku TOTEM: Void and Height
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/sankai-juku-totem-void-and-hei
 ght
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
