DTEND:20261119T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Ballet BC transforms a theater full of strangers into a single\
 , collective audience response—a gasp\, a silence\, a moment of awe.\n\n
  \n\nThis triple bill explores what it means to be human in relationship t
 o one another\, moving from the vulnerable to the virtuosic\, exploring de
 eply personal stories and moments of quiet intimacy to the exhilaration of
  masses of bodies moving together as one. \n\n \n\nThe evening opens with 
 Obsidian by choreographic collaborators Bobbi Jene Smith and Or Schraiber\
 , whose work has been described as “wild and rebellious.” Artistic Dir
 ector Medhi Walerski’s SWAY follows\, inspired by Emily Dickinson’s po
 em “Hope is the thing with feathers” and set to an original score by A
 drien Cronet\, creating moments as fleeting and precarious as the hope des
 cribed in the poem. The evening concludes with Shahar Binyamini’s BOLERO
  X\, set to Ravel’s Boléro\, that builds with pulsating drive and excit
 ement as the ranks of Ballet BC dancers multiply their forces\, turning th
 e stage into a sweeping\, euphoric\, collective—and culminating in a fin
 ale so extraordinary that a room full of strangers can’t help but respon
 d together.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out
  more and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperformingarts.org/events/ballet
 bc/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:Ballet BC Medhi Walerski\, artistic director
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ballet-bc-medhi-walerski-artis
 tic-director
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
