DESCRIPTION:Holiday traditions have a way of bringing people together. The 
 best ones feel familiar and fresh at the same time.\n\n \n\nDorrance Dance
 ‘s The Nutcracker Suite is set to Duke Ellington and Billy Strayhorn’s
  extraordinary 1960 reinterpretation of the Tchaikovsky score. Part season
 al concert\, part tap ballet\, the production transforms the Sugar Plum Fa
 iry into a slinky Sugar Rum Cherry\, turns the “March of the Toy Soldier
 s” into a swinging brass “Peanut Brittle Brigade\,” and gives the or
 iginal ballet’s pageant of national dances a fresh 21st-century twist. \
 n\n \n\nDrawing on the rich traditions of tap dance to tell the story of o
 ne of the most beloved works in the holiday canon\, The Nutcracker Suite i
 s filled with rhythm\, virtuosity\, humor\, and heart. The result is a per
 formance that celebrates the joy of tradition while reminding us that the 
 stories we return to year after year still evolve.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets
  always $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://c
 arolinaperformingarts.org/events/thenutcrackersuite/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:Dorrance Dance The Nutcracker Suite
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/dorrance-dance-the-nutcracker-
 suite
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
