DESCRIPTION:What do you get when you blend Appalachian bluegrass and old-ti
 me music with Latin American folk traditions including flamenco\, murga\, 
 and candombe? You get Che Apalache’s acclaimed Latingrass! \n\n \n\nFoun
 der Joe Troop grew up in North Carolina and taught music in Buenos Aires a
 fter graduating from UNC. His students became his bandmates: Pau Barjau on
  banjo\, Franco Martino on guitar\, and Omar Ruiz-Lopez on mandolin.\n\n \
 n\nRooted in traditions that span continents\, the band grew out of a will
 ingness to follow interests across languages\, cultures\, and traditions. 
 What emerged is a sound shaped by relationships\, shared experiences\, and
  a genuine openness to learning from one another.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets 
 always $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://ca
 rolinaperformingarts.org/events/cheapalache/
LOCATION:Hill Hall\, Moeser Auditorium
SUMMARY:Che Apalache
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/che-apalache
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
