UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53682723652047
DTSTART:20270423T230000Z
DTEND:20270424T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:What can the human body do? Or maybe\, what can it not do?\n\n 
 \n\nIn DO NOT TRY THIS AT HOME\, STREB performers—called “Action Heroe
 s”—dive\, fling\, flip\, and fall off of massive moving structures wit
 h split-second timing and fearless precision. Audiences gasp\, laugh\, ten
 se up\, and wonder how what they’re seeing is even possible.\n\n \n\nFou
 nder Elizabeth Streb has been called the Evel Knievel of dance\, a thrill-
 seeker\, and a Superwoman. She is the founder of SLAM—the STREB Lab for 
 Action Mechanics—in Brooklyn\, where her company has spent decades devel
 oping a movement practice called PopAction: a fusion acrobatics\, rodeo\, 
 dance and athletics\, rooted in a lifelong obsession with what happens to 
 the human body when it is fully\, fearlessly committed to motion. Her phil
 osophy: “Anything too safe is not action.”\n\n \n\nThe company transfo
 rms physical risk into spectacles of wonder\, exploring the outer extremes
  of human movement\, asking what becomes possible when courage\, creativit
 y\, athleticism\, and engineering collide.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always 
 $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out more and buy tickets at: https://carolinap
 erformingarts.org/events/streb/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:STREB EXTREME ACTION DO NOT TRY THIS AT HOME
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/streb-extreme-action-do-not-tr
 y-this-at-home
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
